TITLE:: PltUmwelt
summary:: One spectrum as several listeners receive it
categories:: Libraries>PlotLib
related:: Overviews/PlotLib, Classes/PltObservers, Classes/PltSpectrum

DESCRIPTION::
A long-term average spectrum, drawn faintly in every panel, and over it what one
listener receives of it: the bins of a coarser FFT, mel bands and the curve 13 MFCCs
keep of them, the A-weighted spectrum with what the weighting takes away, the spectral
centroid as a single line. What lies outside a listener's world is shaded.

The reference is itself one listener, an 8192-point FFT averaged over the file.

Listeners are Events:
DEFINITIONLIST::
## code::(type: \fft, size: 512):: || each coarse bin takes the loudest fine bin in
it, so two partials sharing a bin become one. Below one bin width nothing is
resolved.
## code::(type: \mel, bands: 40, coeffs: 13, lo: 20, hi: 16000):: || mean power per
triangular band, then through a DCT and back from the first code::coeffs::.
## code::(type: \aweight):: || IEC 61672 A-weighting, the default of most meters.
## code::(type: \centroid):: || one number.
## code::(type: \band, lo: 300, hi: 3400, name: "telephone"):: || a passband.
::

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: fromSoundFile
argument:: path
argument:: listeners
argument:: fftSize
Of the reference.
argument:: title
argument:: width
argument:: height

METHOD:: new
argument:: spectrum
Magnitudes from 0 Hz to Nyquist.
argument:: sampleRate
argument:: listeners
argument:: title
argument:: width
argument:: height

METHOD:: average
Mean power per bin over frames, as a magnitude.
METHOD:: aWeight
A-weighting in dB, 0 at 1 kHz.
METHOD:: mel
METHOD:: melHz
METHOD:: melBank
METHOD:: melEnergies
Mean power per band in dB, so a band reads on the scale of a bin.
METHOD:: dct
METHOD:: idct
METHOD:: defaultListeners

